WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:03.549
Let's briefly talk about Unreal Engine

2
00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:06.200
as it applies to game development.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.740
Unreal Engine has always fundamentally been a game

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.619
engine, allows you to create content,

5
00:00:11.619 --> 00:00:14.400
let players move around and interact with it,

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.440
and ultimately allow this dynamic exchange between what

7
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.500
the player wants to do and an experience

8
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.179
that you create for them.

9
00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:24.940
There are many benefits to using Unreal Engine for game

10
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.059
development.

11
00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.379
But as it pertains to Sequencer,

12
00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:30.059
the most important thing to remember

13
00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:32.979
is that we are building this world for the players

14
00:00:32.979 --> 00:00:35.140
to interact with, and then occasionally stepping

15
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.600
in to present them with a visual experience

16
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.340
or a montage of images, sound, et cetera.

17
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.679
And we do that predominantly through Sequencer.

18
00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.359
One of the important things that we

19
00:00:48.359 --> 00:00:51.960
want to discuss as we go throughout this course

20
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.859
is the concept of how games are made, released,

21
00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:58.200
and content patched into it.

22
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.799
So throughout this process of building our sequence,

23
00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:05.079
you'll find that we will do certain practices

24
00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:08.780
to keep good organization and structure, keeping in mind

25
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.019
that typically during a video game,

26
00:01:11.019 --> 00:01:14.540
you're going to have several cinematic experiences, meaning

27
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.140
you want to have a very strong, flexible,

28
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.980
and adaptable pipeline and process

29
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.459
for building your sequences and running them or executing

30
00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:27.260
them in the final game.
